# MealHQ platform rule

Before broad codebase exploration, prefer project docs:

- `docs/PLATFORM_BLUEPRINT.md` (primary — requirements, mermaid flows, ADRs, known issues)
- `docs/FUNCTIONAL.md` (product / journeys / business rules)
- `docs/TECHNICAL.md` (API, modules, env, runbook)
- `memory/INDEX.md` and `memory/PRD.md` (short pointers)
- `AGENTS.md` (agent contract)

## Product

- Brand: **MealHQ** (user-facing + API title). Infra IDs may still be `zorvia-*` (GCP, DB name, secrets).
- Multi-tenant tiffin SaaS: provider admin + consumer; `tenant_id = provider_id`.
- Frontend: **Next.js** App Router (TypeScript) in `frontend/`. Platform admin: `admin-frontend/` (dashboard, tenants, inbox, SaaS review, reports).

## Do not reinvent

- Waves A–D shipped (staff/roles, Stripe-optional billing, audit, GST/HST, brand rename).
- SaaS activate: `BILLING_PROVIDER=none` | `stripe` | `manual` (Interac + optimistic activate + admin review).
- Notifications inbox **API** exists; inbox **UI** still deferred.
- Menu (anytime upload + history; consumer sees current/latest): in-app + email + Meta WhatsApp Cloud API share (platform number); see `docs/WHATSAPP_SETUP.md`. WhatsApp is **prepaid** (not in subscription; Interac top-up + admin settle; one successful share per menu). Product UI/APIs gated by `WHATSAPP_FEATURES_ENABLED` (default off). Chat inbox still deferred.
- Activity logs have writers + More-page UI (Wave D).
- Firebase: `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PATH` or `_JSON` + frontend `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_*` (`mealhq-ca`).

## Engineering constraints

- Never commit `.env` or `backend/secrets/`.
- Do **not** deploy to production (Cloud Run / Vercel) or create git commits unless the user explicitly asks.
- Preserve `data-testid`.
- Keep Resend / R2 / Firebase / Stripe / WhatsApp graceful when unset.
- Update docs when behavior changes.
- UI: follow `design_guidelines.json` when editing frontend visuals.
